.TH PCC 1 "July 6, 2026" "ReBSD"
.SH NAME
pcc, cc, cpp \- ReBSD Portable C Compiler driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcc
[
.I option
\&...
]
.I file
\&...
.br
.B cc
[
.I option
\&...
]
.I file
\&...
.br
.B cpp
[
.I option
\&...
]
.I file
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcc
is the ReBSD native C compiler driver.
It runs the PCC preprocessor, compiler, assembler, and linker as needed
for each input file.
.B cc
is the system C compiler name and invokes the same driver.
When invoked as
.B cpp
the driver stops after preprocessing.
.PP
Files ending in
.B .c
are preprocessed, compiled, assembled, and linked.
Files ending in
.B .S
are preprocessed and assembled.
Files ending in
.B .s
are assembled.
Files ending in
.B .o
and archives are passed to the linker.
.PP
On a ReBSD target the default sysroot is
.IR / .
The default link includes the ReBSD start file and the standard libraries
.BR \-lpcc ,
.BR \-lc ,
and
.BR \-lpcc .
The default MIPS CPU and floating-point ABI are selected when the rootfs or
standalone SDK compiler is built, and may be overridden with the MIPS options
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Compile or assemble input files and stop after producing object files.
.TP
.B \-S
Compile input files and stop after producing assembler output.
.TP
.B \-E
Preprocess input files and write the result to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write the final output, or the single requested intermediate output, to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Add
.I dir
to the preprocessor include search path.
.TP
.BI \-D " name"
.TQ
.BI \-D " name=value"
Define a preprocessor macro.
.TP
.BI \-U " name"
Undefine a preprocessor macro.
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
Add
.I dir
to the library search path used by the linker.
.TP
.BI \-l " name"
Link with
.BI lib name .a
from the library search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot= dir
Use
.I dir
as the root for standard include and library directories.
If no sysroot is specified on a ReBSD target,
.I /
is used.
.TP
.B \-nostdinc
Do not search the standard system include directories.
.TP
.B \-nostartfiles
Do not pass the standard start files to the linker.
.TP
.B \-nodefaultlibs
Do not pass the default libraries to the linker.
.TP
.B \-nostdlib
Do not pass standard start files or default libraries to the linker.
.TP
.BI \-Wa, option
Pass
.I option
to
.BR as (1).
.TP
.BI \-Wl, option
Pass
.I option
to
.BR ld (1).
.TP
.BI \-Wp, option
Pass
.I option
to the preprocessor.
.TP
.BI \-Wc, option
Pass
.I option
to the compiler proper.
.TP
.B \-mips3
.TQ
.B \-march=vr4300
Select the VR4300\-compatible MIPS code generation mode used by the N64
and Malta64 compatibility ports.
This mode uses the older MIPS III instruction set and the ReBSD VR4300
8-byte aggregate alignment policy.
.TP
.B \-mips32r2
.TQ
.B \-march=mips32r2
Select the MIPS32 revision 2 code generation mode used by the Malta port.
This mode enables MIPS32r2 instruction selection, passes
.B \-march=mips32r2
to
.BR as (1),
and uses the Malta o32 4-byte aggregate alignment policy.
.TP
.B \-mhard\-float
.TQ
.B \-msoft\-float
Select hardware or software floating\-point code generation when supported
by the target configuration.
Hard-float mode defines
.B __mips_hard_float
and uses
.IR /usr/lib/libpcc.a .
Soft-float mode defines
.B __mips_soft_float
and searches
.I /usr/lib/softfloat
before the normal system library directory so soft-float helper routines are
taken from
.IR /usr/lib/softfloat/libpcc.a .
.TP
.B \-g
Request debug information.
.TP
.BI \-O level
Select an optimization level.
.TP
.B \-v
Print commands as they are run.  When no input files are supplied, print the
compiler version and target information and exit successfully.
.TP
.B \-\&#\&#\&#
Print the commands that would be run, but do not execute them.
.SH TARGET MODES
The current ReBSD
.B mips-rebsd
PCC target is big-endian o32.  Endianness is selected when PCC is built; the
current target does not accept a runtime little-endian mode.  A future mipsel
port should use a separate compiler target.
.PP
The CPU option is passed to both the compiler proper and the assembler.  This
keeps generated instructions, assembler instruction checks, and C ABI layout in
the same mode.  Mixing VR4300 objects and MIPS32r2 objects in one rootfs is not
a supported ABI.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/pcc/cpp
PCC preprocessor.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/pcc/ccom
PCC C compiler proper.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/as
Assembler.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/ld
Link editor.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/crt0.o
Program start file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/libpcc.a
PCC runtime helper library.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/softfloat/libpcc.a
Soft-float PCC runtime helper library.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/libc.a
System C library.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/libm.a
System math library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR as (1),
.BR ld (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR ranlib (1),
.BR size (1)
